(a) Application to the building inspector for a building permit shall be made in writing on a form provided for the purpose. The application must be accompanied by a plan drawn to scale showing the following items in sufficient detail to enable the building inspector to ascertain whether the proposed excavation, construction, moving, or alteration is in conformance with this chapter:
(1) The shape, size, and location of the lot to be built upon;
(2) The shapes, height, uses, and locations on the lot of buildings or structures to be erected or altered;
(3) The sizes, locations, and uses of all existing buildings or structures on the lot;
(4) The number of dwelling units the building is designed to accommodate, if any;
(5) The setback lines of buildings on adjoining lots;
(6) The layout of off-street parking spaces;
(7) Such other information concerning the lot or adjoining lots as may be essential for determining whether the provisions of this chapter are being observed.
(b) If the proposed excavation, filling, construction, moving, or alteration as set forth is in conformity with the provisions of the code then in force, the building inspector shall issue a building permit. If a building permit is not approved, the building inspector shall state such refusal in writing, including the cause for disapproval.
(c) The building permit shall contain at least the following information:
(1) The name and address of the applicant;
(2) The block or street number of the lot to which the permit applies;
(3) The zoning district in which the property is located;
(4) Whether the permit authorizes excavation, filling, construction, moving, or alteration and the type of structure being built;
(5) The date of the application;
(6) The signatures of the applicant and the building inspector.
(d) Before commencing excavation, filling, construction, moving, or alteration, the building permit, or a copy thereof, shall be placed in a conspicuous location on or near the front of the property for the duration of the excavation, filling, construction, moving, or alteration, and in such a manner that it is protected from the weather.
(Code 2007, § 14-2.1)

